\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Figure 1.} Model architecture. A one-layer, single-head causal transformer with embedding dimension \(d = 2\), context window \(T = 8\), and a 12-token vocabulary. The token embeddings \(\mathbf  {X}\) and positional embeddings \(\mathbf  {P}\) of the \(T\) positions (each \(8 \times 2\), one row per position) are summed to give \(\mathbf  {E} = \mathbf  {X} + \mathbf  {P}\). Self-attention (yellow) projects \(\mathbf  {E}\) into queries, keys and values, \(\mathbf  {Q} = \mathbf  {E}\mathbf  {W}_Q^\top \), \(\mathbf  {K} = \mathbf  {E}\mathbf  {W}_K^\top \) and \(\mathbf  {V} = \mathbf  {E}\mathbf  {W}_V^\top \), each with a \(2 \times 2\) weight matrix. The scaled scores \(\mathbf  {Q}\mathbf  {K}^\top /\sqrt  {d_k}\) are causally masked and softmax-normalized to give the \(8 \times 8\) attention weights \(\mathbf  {A}\), and the attention output is \(\mathbf  {A}\mathbf  {V}\). A residual connection (green) adds \(\mathbf  {E}\) to this output, giving \(\mathbf  {Z}\). A position-wise feed-forward network (red; Linear(2,32), ReLU, Linear(32,2)) is applied to \(\mathbf  {Z}\), and a second residual connection (blue) adds \(\mathbf  {Z}\) back, giving the final hidden states \(\mathbf  {H}\). The language-model head (green; Linear(2,12)) followed by a softmax maps each row of \(\mathbf  {H}\) to a probability distribution over the next token (\(8 \times 12\)). The figure shows the shape of each matrix next to it.}}{4}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
